tools.description:
Add one or more tasks to a project, section, or parent. Supports assignment to project collaborators.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__add_tasks(args: {
// The array of tasks to add (max 100).
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 100
tasks: Array<
{
// The task name/title. Should be concise and actionable (e.g., "Review PR #123", "Call dentist"). For longer content, use the description field instead. Supports Markdown.
content: string, // minLength: 1
// The deadline date for the task in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD, e.g., "2025-12-31"). Deadlines are immovable constraints shown with a different indicator than due dates.
deadlineDate?: string,
// Additional details, notes, or context for the task. Use this for longer content rather than putting it in the task name. Supports Markdown.
description?: string,
// The due date for the task, in natural language. Also use natural language for recurrences; do not prefix it with "recurring".
dueString?: string,
// The duration of the task. Use format: "2h" (hours), "90m" (minutes), "2h30m" (combined), "1.5h" (decimal hours), or "3d" (whole days; days cannot be combined with hours or minutes). Todoist apps only display durations under 24 hours: a longer or day-based duration is stored and reported by this server, but the apps show the task as having no duration.
duration?: string,
// Whether this task should be uncompletable (organizational header). Tasks with isUncompletable: true appear as organizational headers and cannot be completed.
isUncompletable?: boolean,
// The labels to attach to the task.
labels?: string[], // maxItems: 50
// Position of the task among sibling tasks under the same parent/section.
order?: number,
// The parent task ID (for subtasks).
parentId?: string,
// Task priority as a string: "p1" (highest), "p2" (high), "p3" (medium), or "p4" (lowest/default). Integers like 1, 2, 3, or 4 are not accepted.
priority?: "p1" | "p2" | "p3" | "p4",
// The project ID to add this task to. Project ID should be an ID string, or the text "inbox", for inbox tasks.
projectId?: string,
// Assign task to this user. Can be "me" (assigns to current user), a user ID, name, or email address. User must be a collaborator on the target project.
responsibleUser?: string,
// The section ID to add this task to.
sectionId?: string,
}
>,
}): Promise<{
failureCount: number,
// Tasks that could not be created, with the reason for each.
failures: Array<
{
code?: string,
error: string,
// Usually the ID of the item that failed.
item: string,
}
>,
successCount: number,
// The created tasks.
tasks: Array<
{
// ISO 8601.
addedAt?: string,
assignedByUid?: string,
// Whether the task is completed.
checked: boolean,
// ISO 8601.
completedAt?: string,
// Task title.
content: string,
// ISO 8601.
deadlineDate?: string,
description: string,
// ISO 8601.
dueDate?: string,
// e.g. "2h30m", or "3d" for a day-based duration.
duration?: string,
id: string,
// True when deleted; absent otherwise.
isDeleted?: boolean,
// An organizational header, not a real task.
isUncompletable?: boolean,
labels?: string[],
parentId?: string,
// p1 is highest, p4 lowest.
priority: "p1" | "p2" | "p3" | "p4",
projectId: string,
// False when not recurring, otherwise the recurrence string.
recurring: boolean | string,
responsibleUid?: string,
sectionId?: string,
}
>,
// The total number of tasks created.
totalCount: number,
totalRequested: number,
}>;
```

Trigger a new health analysis for a project. Use this when the health data is stale or you want a fresh assessment. The analysis may take time to complete — use get-project-health afterward to see updated results.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__analyze_project_health(args: {
// The ID of the project to analyze. This triggers a new health analysis which may take some time to complete.
projectId: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<{
// The health response returned after triggering analysis.
health: {
// Whether the health data is still stale after the request.
isStale: boolean,
// The health status after triggering analysis.
status: "UNKNOWN" | "ON_TRACK" | "AT_RISK" | "CRITICAL" | "EXCELLENT" | "ERROR",
// Whether an analysis update is currently in progress.
updateInProgress: boolean,
},
// A human-readable message about the analysis status.
message: string,
// The project ID.
projectId: string,
}>;
```

Complete one or more tasks by their IDs.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__complete_tasks(args: {
// The IDs of the tasks to complete.
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 50
ids: Array<
string // minLength: 1
>,
}): Promise<{
// The IDs of successfully completed tasks.
completed: string[],
// The number of failed task completions.
failureCount: number,
// Failed task completions with error details.
failures: Array<
{
code?: string,
error: string,
// Usually the ID of the item that failed.
item: string,
}
>,
// The number of successfully completed tasks.
successCount: number,
// The total number of tasks requested to complete.
totalRequested: number,
}>;
```

Delete a project, section, task, comment, label, filter, folder, reminder, or location_reminder by its ID. Projects can be deleted whether active or archived (find archived ones via find-projects with archivedStatus); note a workspace project must be archived before it can be deleted, while personal projects can be deleted regardless. Deleting a folder keeps its projects, moving them to the top level of the workspace.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__delete_object(args: {
// The ID of the entity to delete.
id: string, // minLength: 1
// The type of entity to delete.
type: "project" | "section" | "task" | "comment" | "label" | "filter" | "folder" | "reminder" | "location_reminder",
}): Promise<{
// Information about the deleted entity.
deletedEntity: {
// The ID of the deleted entity.
id: string,
// The type of deleted entity.
type: "project" | "section" | "task" | "comment" | "label" | "filter" | "folder" | "reminder" | "location_reminder",
},
// Whether the deletion was successful.
success: boolean,
}>;
```

Export an existing project as a Todoist template, either as CSV content or as a shareable URL. Use it to duplicate a project, share its structure, or hand the CSV to import-project-template. To read a project rather than export it, use find-tasks instead — it returns structured tasks rather than raw CSV. The project itself is not modified, but the "url" format uploads a copy and returns a link that anyone holding it can open.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__export_project_template(args: {
// How to return the template. "file" returns the CSV content, which can be passed straight back to import-project-template. "url" returns a shareable download link instead, and is the better choice for large projects because it does not return the whole file.
format?: "file" | "url", // default: "file"
// The ID of the project to export as a template.
projectId: string, // minLength: 1
// Export due dates relative to the import date (e.g. "day 3") instead of absolute dates. Defaults to false.
useRelativeDates?: boolean,
}): Promise<{
// The template as CSV content. Only present when format is "file".
content?: string,
// The generated template file name. Only present when format is "url".
fileName?: string,
// The shareable download URL. Only present when format is "url".
fileUrl?: string,
// The format the template was exported in.
format: "file" | "url",
// Number of rows in the exported CSV. Only present when format is "file".
lineCount?: number,
}>;
```

Fetch the full contents of a task or project by its ID. The ID should be in the format "task:{id}" or "project:{id}". (Comments may exist; use find-comments to retrieve them.)

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__fetch(args: {
// A unique identifier for the document in the format "task:{id}" or "project:{id}".
id: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<{
// The ID of the fetched document.
id: string,
// Additional metadata about the document.
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
metadata?: { [key: string]: any },
// The text content of the document.
text: string,
// The title of the document.
title: string,
// The URL of the document.
url: string,
}>;
```

Fetch a single task, project, comment, or section by its ID. Use this when you have a specific object ID and want to retrieve its full details. Set includeChildren to also get its direct subtasks or sub-projects.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__fetch_object(args: {
// The unique ID of the object to fetch.
id: string, // minLength: 1
// Also return the direct children of the object: subtasks for a task, sub-projects for a project. Returns childCount plus a compact list, flagging each child that has children of its own. Use this to check whether a task hides subtasks instead of a speculative find-tasks lookup. Ignored for comments and sections.
includeChildren?: boolean,
// The type of object to fetch.
type: "task" | "project" | "comment" | "section",
}): Promise<{
// The number of direct children listed in children. Only present when children were requested and the type supports them. 0 means the object definitively has none.
childCount?: number,
// Direct children only: subtasks for a task, sub-projects for a project. Completed subtasks and archived sub-projects are excluded.
children?: Array<

 | {
// Whether the task is completed.
checked: boolean,
// Task title.
content: string,
// ISO 8601.
dueDate?: string,
// Whether this subtask has subtasks of its own. Fetch it with includeChildren to expand.
hasChildren: boolean,
id: string,
}
 | {
// Whether this sub-project has sub-projects of its own. Fetch it with includeChildren to expand.
hasChildren: boolean,
id: string,
name: string,
}

>,
// Present when the children lookup failed or returned incomplete information. When no children are listed alongside it, childCount is unknown - do not read its absence as "no children".
childrenError?: string,
// Present when the object has more than 25 direct children and the list was truncated. Page through the rest with find-tasks by parentId for subtasks, or find-projects for sub-projects.
hasMoreChildren?: boolean,
// The ID of the fetched object.
id: string,
// The fetched object data.
object:
 | {
// ISO 8601.
addedAt?: string,
assignedByUid?: string,
// Whether the task is completed.
checked: boolean,
// ISO 8601.
completedAt?: string,
// Task title.
content: string,
// ISO 8601.
deadlineDate?: string,
description: string,
// ISO 8601.
dueDate?: string,
// e.g. "2h30m", or "3d" for a day-based duration.
duration?: string,
id: string,
// True when deleted; absent otherwise.
isDeleted?: boolean,
// An organizational header, not a real task.
isUncompletable?: boolean,
labels?: string[],
parentId?: string,
// p1 is highest, p4 lowest.
priority: "p1" | "p2" | "p3" | "p4",
projectId: string,
// False when not recurring, otherwise the recurrence string.
recurring: boolean | string,
responsibleUid?: string,
sectionId?: string,
}
 | {
// Ordering index among siblings.
childOrder: number,
color?: "berry_red" | "red" | "orange" | "yellow" | "olive_green" | "lime_green" | "green" | "mint_green" | "teal" | "sky_blue" | "light_blue" | "blue" | "grape" | "violet" | "lavender" | "magenta" | "salmon" | "charcoal" | "grey" | "taupe",
// Empty string when none.
description: string,
// Workspace projects only.
folderId?: string,
icon?: string,
id: string,
inboxProject: boolean,
isArchived: boolean,
isFavorite: boolean,
isShared: boolean,
name: string,
parentId?: string,
// list, board, calendar or table.
viewStyle: string,
// Undefined for personal projects.
workspaceId?: string,
}
 | {
content: string,
fileAttachment?: {
// Milliseconds, for audio/video.
fileDuration?: number,
fileName?: string,
// Bytes.
fileSize?: number,
// MIME type.
fileType?: string,
fileUrl?: string,
// For image resource types.
image?: string,
// Pixels.
imageHeight?: number,
// Pixels.
imageWidth?: number,
// file, url, image, etc.
resourceType: string,
// For link/url resource types.
title?: string,
uploadState?: "pending" | "completed",
// For link/url resource types.
url?: string,
},
id: string,
// Users notified about this comment. Absent when nobody was notified.
notifiedUserIds?: string[],
// ISO 8601.
postedAt: string,
postedUid?: string,
projectId?: string,
taskId?: string,
}
 | {
// Supports Markdown.
description?: string,
id: string,
name: string,
// Ordering index within the project.
sectionOrder: number,
}
,
// The type of object fetched.
type: "task" | "project" | "comment" | "section",
}>;
```

Retrieve activity logs to monitor and audit changes in Todoist. Shows events from all users by default (use initiatorId to filter by specific user). To answer what someone completed in a period, including recurring task occurrences, use objectType "task", eventType "completed", and dateFrom/dateTo. For a first-person question ("what did I get done"), also set initiatorId to the current user from user-info, or the answer includes collaborators' completions. Track task completions, updates, deletions, project changes, and more with flexible filtering. Activity history availability and retention depend on the user plan.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_activity(args: {
// Pagination cursor for retrieving the next page of results.
cursor?: string,
// Inclusive start of the activity range, as an ISO 8601 date or date-time. For all events on one local calendar day, use that day's start, for example "2026-08-02T00:00:00-04:00". Natural-language dates such as "tomorrow" are not supported.
dateFrom?: string,
// Exclusive end of the activity range, as an ISO 8601 date or date-time. For all events on 2026-08-02, use "2026-08-03T00:00:00-04:00". Natural-language dates such as "tomorrow" are not supported.
dateTo?: string,
// Type of event to filter by.
eventType?: "added" | "updated" | "deleted" | "completed" | "uncompleted" | "archived" | "unarchived" | "shared" | "left" | "moved",
// Filter by the user ID who initiated the event. A first-person question ("what did I complete") needs this: without it the results cover every collaborator. Get the ID from user-info when you do not already have it.
initiatorId?: string,
// Maximum number of activity events to return.
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Filter by specific object ID (task, project, or comment). Requires objectType.
objectId?: string,
// Type of object to filter by.
objectType?: "task" | "comment" | "project",
// Filter events by parent project ID.
projectId?: string,
// Filter events by parent task ID (for subtask events).
taskId?: string,
}): Promise<{
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
appliedFilters: { [key: string]: any },
// The activity events.
events: Array<
{
// ISO 8601.
eventDate: string,
// added, updated, deleted, completed, etc.
eventType: string,
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
extraData?: { [key: string]: any },
id?: string,
// User who initiated the event.
initiatorId?: string,
objectId: string,
// task, project, etc.
objectType: string,
parentItemId?: string,
parentProjectId?: string,
}
>,
hasMore: boolean,
nextCursor?: string,
// The total number of events in this page.
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

Find comments by task, project, or get a specific comment by ID. Exactly one of taskId, projectId, or commentId must be provided.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_comments(args: {
// Get a specific comment by ID.
commentId?: string,
// Pagination cursor for retrieving more results.
cursor?: string,
// Maximum number of comments to return
limit?: integer, // minimum: 1, maximum: 10
// Find comments for a specific project. Project ID should be an ID string, or the text "inbox", for inbox tasks.
projectId?: string,
// Find comments for a specific task.
taskId?: string,
}): Promise<{
// The found comments.
comments: Array<
{
content: string,
fileAttachment?: {
// Milliseconds, for audio/video.
fileDuration?: number,
fileName?: string,
// Bytes.
fileSize?: number,
// MIME type.
fileType?: string,
fileUrl?: string,
// For image resource types.
image?: string,
// Pixels.
imageHeight?: number,
// Pixels.
imageWidth?: number,
// file, url, image, etc.
resourceType: string,
// For link/url resource types.
title?: string,
uploadState?: "pending" | "completed",
// For link/url resource types.
url?: string,
},
id: string,
// Users notified about this comment. Absent when nobody was notified.
notifiedUserIds?: string[],
// ISO 8601.
postedAt: string,
postedUid?: string,
projectId?: string,
taskId?: string,
}
>,
hasMore: boolean,
nextCursor?: string,
// The ID that was searched for (comment, task, or project ID).
searchId: string,
// The type of search performed: "single" (comment ID), "task" (task ID), or "project" (project ID).
searchType: string,
// The total number of comments in this page.
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

Get completed tasks in a date range. Neither getBy mode returns completions of a recurring task that is still active. For "what did I complete/get done" questions, or whenever recurring work should count, use find-activity instead — it reports completion events, including every occurrence of a recurring task. since/until are optional and default to a 7-day window when omitted. Includes all collaborators by default. Person-specific queries (summaries, plans, reports) require responsibleUser.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_completed_tasks(args: {
// The cursor to get the next page of tasks (cursor is obtained from the previous call to this tool, with the same parameters).
cursor?: string,
// The method to use to get the tasks: "completion" to get tasks by completion date (ie, when the task was actually completed), "due" to get tasks by due date (ie, when the task was due to be completed by).
getBy?: "completion" | "due", // default: "completion"
// The labels to filter the tasks by
labels?: string[], // maxItems: 50
// The operator to use when filtering by labels. This will dictate whether a task has all labels, or some of them. Default is "or".
labelsOperator?: "and" | "or",
// The maximum number of tasks to return.
limit?: integer, // default: 50, minimum: 1, maximum: 200
// The ID of the parent task to get the tasks for.
parentId?: string,
// The ID of the project to get the tasks for. Project ID should be an ID string, or the text "inbox", for inbox tasks.
projectId?: string,
// Filter completed tasks assigned to this user. User ID, name, or email. For personal queries (summaries, plans, reports), set to current user from user-info to exclude collaborators. Defaults to all collaborators.
responsibleUser?: string,
// The ID of the section to get the tasks for.
sectionId?: string,
// Optional start date for completed tasks. Format: YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to 6 days before until (or today if until is omitted), resulting in a 7-day window.
since?: string, // pattern: /^(?:(?:\d\d[2468][048]|\d\d[13579][26]|\d\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\d|2[0-8])))$/, format: "date"
// Optional end date for completed tasks. Format: YYYY-MM-DD. Defaults to 6 days after since (or today if since is omitted), resulting in a 7-day window.
until?: string, // pattern: /^(?:(?:\d\d[2468][048]|\d\d[13579][26]|\d\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\d|2[0-8])))$/, format: "date"
// The ID of the workspace to get the tasks for.
workspaceId?: string,
}): Promise<{
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
appliedFilters: { [key: string]: any },
hasMore: boolean,
nextCursor?: string,
// The found completed tasks.
tasks: Array<
{
// ISO 8601.
addedAt?: string,
assignedByUid?: string,
// Whether the task is completed.
checked: boolean,
// ISO 8601.
completedAt?: string,
// Task title.
content: string,
// ISO 8601.
deadlineDate?: string,
description: string,
// ISO 8601.
dueDate?: string,
// e.g. "2h30m", or "3d" for a day-based duration.
duration?: string,
id: string,
// True when deleted; absent otherwise.
isDeleted?: boolean,
// An organizational header, not a real task.
isUncompletable?: boolean,
labels?: string[],
parentId?: string,
// p1 is highest, p4 lowest.
priority: "p1" | "p2" | "p3" | "p4",
projectId: string,
// False when not recurring, otherwise the recurrence string.
recurring: boolean | string,
responsibleUid?: string,
sectionId?: string,
}
>,
// The total number of tasks in this page.
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

List all personal filters or search for filters by name. Filters are saved custom views that use query syntax to organize tasks (e.g. "today & p1", "#Work & overdue").

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_filters(args: {
// Search for a filter by name (partial and case insensitive match). If omitted, all filters are returned.
search?: string,
}): Promise<{
// The found filters.
filters: Array<
{
color?: "berry_red" | "red" | "orange" | "yellow" | "olive_green" | "lime_green" | "green" | "mint_green" | "teal" | "sky_blue" | "light_blue" | "blue" | "grape" | "violet" | "lavender" | "magenta" | "salmon" | "charcoal" | "grey" | "taupe",
// A markdown description explaining what the filter is for. Omitted when the filter has none.
description?: string,
// The unique ID of the filter.
id: string,
// Whether the filter is marked as favorite.
isFavorite: boolean,
// The display order of the filter.
itemOrder: number,
// The name of the filter.
name: string,
// The filter query string (e.g. "today & p1", "#Work & overdue").
query: string,
}
>,
// The total number of filters returned.
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

List the folders that group a workspace's projects. Only workspace projects go in folders; personal projects nest under a parent project instead. To see a folder's projects, use find-projects with folderId.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_folders(args: {
// The workspace to list folders for, by name or ID (see list-workspaces). Omit to list the folders of every workspace.
workspace?: string, // minLength: 1
}): Promise<{
// In sidebar order within each workspace.
folders: { id: string, name: string, workspaceId: string }[],
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

List personal labels and shared labels. Personal labels have full metadata (id, name, color, order, isFavorite) and support pagination and name search (partial, case insensitive). Shared labels are labels used on tasks shared with you — they are returned as names only (no IDs or metadata). When searching, all matching personal labels are fetched across all pages and returned as a single result set (limit and cursor are ignored). When not searching, personal labels are returned with pagination.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_labels(args: {
// The cursor to get the next page of labels (cursor is obtained from the previous call to this tool, with the same parameters). Ignored when searchText is provided.
cursor?: string,
// The maximum number of labels to return.
limit?: integer, // default: 50, minimum: 1, maximum: 200
// Search for a label by name (partial and case insensitive match). Supports wildcards (e.g. "work*" for prefix match). Use "\*" for a literal asterisk. If omitted, all labels are returned.
searchText?: string,
}): Promise<{
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
appliedFilters: { [key: string]: any },
hasMore: boolean,
// The found personal labels.
labels: Array<
{
color?: "berry_red" | "red" | "orange" | "yellow" | "olive_green" | "lime_green" | "green" | "mint_green" | "teal" | "sky_blue" | "light_blue" | "blue" | "grape" | "violet" | "lavender" | "magenta" | "salmon" | "charcoal" | "grey" | "taupe",
id: string,
isFavorite: boolean,
name: string,
// Display order.
order?: number,
}
>,
nextCursor?: string,
// Names of all shared labels visible to you. These have no IDs or metadata — use their names directly when filtering tasks.
sharedLabels: string[],
// The total number of labels in this page.
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

Find Todoist users (collaborators, teammates) by name or email to look up their user ID. Use this whenever the user asks to find, look up, or identify a person — e.g. "find Carrie's user ID", "who is Ernesto", "look up a user". When projectId is omitted, searches across the collaborators of every shared project the authenticated user has access to, plus the authenticated user themselves — an empty result means the person is not a collaborator on any project you share with them, not necessarily that they do not exist in Todoist. When projectId is provided, searches only that project. Partial, case-insensitive match on name and email.

```ts
mcp__Todoist__To_Do_List___Calendar__find_project_collaborators(args: {
// Optional. If provided, searches only collaborators of this project. If omitted, searches across the collaborators of all shared projects the authenticated user can access (plus the authenticated user themselves) — use this for general "find a user" / "who is X" lookups.
projectId?: string, // minLength: 1
// Search for a user by name or email (partial and case insensitive match). If omitted, all users are returned.
searchTerm?: string,
}): Promise<{
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
appliedFilters: { [key: string]: any },
// The found users.
collaborators: { email: string, id: string, name: string }[],
// Information about the project (only present when projectId was provided).
projectInfo?: {
// The project ID.
id: string,
// Whether the project is shared.
isShared: boolean,
// The project name.
name: string,
},
// The total number of available users before the search filter was applied.
totalAvailable?: number,
// The total number of users found.
totalCount: number,
}>;
```

