## What this tool does
Computes aggregate measures (counts, averages, sums, NPS scores, and more) for a single field or an entire dataset.

Call insights-public_discover first to resolve form_id / audience_id / study_id / field_id / property_id and to
learn each field's filter_type, filter_operators, and filter_values before filtering.
For a study, field_id is the question's ref, and task_ref with field_id null returns a usability task's matrix
(participants by AI verdict and by their own answer). Screener questions' counts include participants who were screened
out. New sessions appear after a short delay.

## Use when
- User asks for summary statistics, totals, averages, counts, or scores
- User wants aggregated data rather than individual rows
- User asks about NPS score, response count, average rating, or similar rolled-up metrics

## Also known as
summary statistics, totals, counts, averages, sums, NPS scores, aggregate analytics, rolled-up metrics

## Constraints
- Provide exactly one of form_id, audience_id or study_id — never more than one, never none. task_ref needs study_id.
- Optional parameters may be omitted or sent as null.
- variable_name needs study_id and field_id; it counts the conversations that have a value for that variable, as one total. Use toplist for the per-category breakdown.

## Frequency analysis (studies)
- An open-ended study question is analysed through its categorical variables: pass study_id, field_id and variable_name (one of the field's variables in insights-public_discover).
  Aggregate returns one total; toplist returns each category as the answer_choice_label dimension.
- To drill down, filter a child variable by a parent's categories: field "answers.<field_id>:<parent_variable>", operator any_of,
  value text_list of the parent's category labels, on the same field_id as the query. Only any_of is supported on variables.
- The drill-down applies only when conditional is "and" at both levels (or the group has one condition) and negate is not set.
  Any other shape filters whole conversations instead of the parent's categories, so the counts differ.

## Supported field types
- forms dataset: text, number, scale, boolean, choices, dropdown, nps, date, multi_format, transcript, payment, matrix, ranking.
- contacts dataset: text, text_list, number.
- studies: choices, dropdown, rating and opinion scale, ranking, open-ended (count only),
  and the usability matrix.


