## What this tool does
Ranks groups of rows by a measure — e.g. "top 5 lead sources by contact count" or "which NPS category has the most responses."

Call insights-public_discover first to resolve form_id / audience_id / study_id / field_id / property_id and to
learn each field's dimensions, measures, filter_type, filter_operators, and filter_values before filtering.
For a study, field_id is the question's ref, and task_ref with field_id null ranks a usability task's matrix
(by ai_assessment and user_assessment). Screener questions' counts include participants who were screened out. New
sessions appear after a short delay.

## Use when
- User asks for a ranking, "top N", breakdown by category, or "most/least common" answer
- User wants rows grouped by one or two dimensions and sorted by a measure
- User wants to compare groups/choices/values against each other, not a single rolled-up number

## Also known as
top N, ranking, leaderboard, breakdown by category, grouped counts, most common, least common

## Constraints
- Provide exactly one of form_id, audience_id or study_id — never more than one, never none. task_ref needs study_id.
- dimensions: 1-2 entries. Each name must be a dimension the selected field supports (see insights-public_discover).
- Optional parameters may be omitted or sent as null.
- variable_name needs study_id and field_id; with it use dimension answer_choice_label and measure count.

## Frequency analysis (studies)
- An open-ended study question is analysed through its categorical variables: pass study_id, field_id and variable_name (one of the field's variables in insights-public_discover).
  Each category the variable can take is returned as the answer_choice_label dimension.
- To drill down, filter a child variable by a parent's categories: field "answers.<field_id>:<parent_variable>", operator any_of,
  value text_list of the parent's category labels, on the same field_id as the query. Only any_of is supported on variables.
- The drill-down applies only when conditional is "and" at both levels (or the group has one condition) and negate is not set.
  Any other shape filters whole conversations instead of the parent's categories, so the counts differ.

## Supported field types
- forms dataset: number, nps, scale, boolean, choices, text_list, payment, dropdown, multi_format, matrix, transcript, ranking.
- contacts dataset: text_list.
- studies: choices, dropdown, rating and opinion scale, ranking, and the usability matrix. Open-ended questions are ranked through their categorical variables
  (see Frequency analysis).


