Use this tool to create a new Typeform Page in a workspace. After creation, the page has no content — use the Typeform Pages draft editing tools to add content.

## What this tool does
- Creates a new page in the specified workspace.
- Creates a default variant alongside the page.
- Returns the page record and its default variant.

## Inputs
- workspace_id: ID of the workspace in which to create the page. The owning account is derived from the workspace.
- title: Human-readable title for the new page.

## Output
- page: the newly created page including its public URLs and builder URL (links, where links.builder is the admin URL to edit the page in the builder).
  - page.links.builder: give this to the user exactly as returned whenever they want to open or edit the page in the builder.
- variant: the default variant created alongside the page.
  - variant.id: pass this as variantId to the Typeform Pages draft editing tools. It is NOT a page ID.

## Notes
- Never construct builder or public URLs yourself. page.id and variant.id are different IDs that look almost identical; builder URLs use the page id, and links.builder already has it right. A builder URL built with variant.id opens a broken builder.
- If links.builder is null (link resolution failed), do not build a URL: call get_page to retry, or tell the user to open the page from the Pages dashboard.
- The new page has no blocks until you add them.
- To see the page in list_pages results, use the workspace_id you supplied here.


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_create_page(args: {
// Human-readable title for the new page.
title: string,
// ID of the workspace in which to create the page. The owning account is derived from the workspace.
workspace_id: string,
}): Promise<{
page: {
// ID of the account that owns this page.
account_id: string,
// When the page was created.
created_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// Unique page identifier.
id: string,
links: {
// Region-aware admin URL where the page is edited in the builder (e.g. https://admin.typeform.com/accounts/{accountId}/pages/{id}/create). Present whether or not the page is live. Null when link resolution fails. Use verbatim; do not construct this URL from page or variant IDs.
builder: string | null,
// Active custom-domain URL. Null when the page is not live, when no active custom-domain route exists, or when link resolution fails.
custom_domain: string | null,
// Default subdomain URL (e.g. https://page.typeform.com/p/{id}). Null only when link resolution fails entirely.
default: string | null,
// The highest-precedence public URL available for this page. Null when the page has no published revision (i.e. the page is not yet live), or when link resolution fails.
display: string | null,
},
// Human-readable page title.
title: string,
// When the page was last updated.
updated_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// ID of the workspace this page belongs to.
workspace_id: string,
},
variant: {
// When the variant was created.
created_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// Unique variant identifier.
id: string,
// Whether this is the page's default variant.
is_default: boolean,
// Human-readable variant label.
label: string,
// ID of the page this variant belongs to.
page_id: string,
// Current publication status of the variant.
publication_status: "empty_draft" | "draft" | "published" | "changed",
// When the variant was last updated.
updated_at: string, // format: "date-time"
},
}>;
```

Use this tool to connect a verified custom domain (and path) to a Typeform Page, so that visiting https://{domain}{path} serves the page.

## What this tool does
- Creates a route that maps domain_id + path to the given page.
- The domain must already be registered and verified. Complete the domain lifecycle first with create_domain and get_domain_status; if the domain is not verified this tool returns DOMAIN_NOT_VERIFIED.
- Idempotent: if the same domain + path is already routed to this page, the existing route is returned with already_existed=true.

## Inputs
- page_id: ID of the page to route the domain to (from list_pages or create_page).
- domain_id: ID of the verified custom domain (from create_domain / get_domain_status).
- path: path on the domain. Either "/" for the domain root, or a single-segment alias of 5-15 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens (e.g. "/spring-sale"). Normalised to lowercase with a leading slash. Invalid paths return VALIDATION_ERROR.

## Output
- route: the route record:
  - route_id, domain_id, hostname, path, url (the full public URL), target_type ("page"), page_id.
  - serves_content: true when the routed page has a published revision and is serving content.
  - created_at, updated_at.
  - already_existed: present, and true, only when the requested domain and path were already routed to this page and no new route was created; omitted otherwise.
  - When serves_content is false, the route exists but visitors see nothing until the page is published with publish_variant.

## Notes
- A page may only use one custom domain. Routing a page that already has routes on another domain returns PAGE_ALREADY_HAS_DOMAIN.
- If the domain + path is already routed to a different page, ROUTE_ALREADY_EXISTS is returned. Use update_page_domain_route or disconnect_page_domain_route on the existing route first.
- Returns DOMAIN_NOT_FOUND when the domain does not exist or is not owned by the page's account.


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_create_page_domain_route(args: {
// ID of the verified custom domain.
domain_id: string,
// ID of the page to route the domain to.
page_id: string,
// Path for the route: "/" for the domain root, or a single-segment alias of 5-15 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens (e.g. "/spring-sale").
path: string,
}): Promise<{
route: {
// Present, and true, only when the requested domain and path were already routed to this page and no new route was created. Omitted otherwise.
already_existed?: boolean,
// When the route was created.
created_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// ID of the custom domain (account-service page domain) this route is on.
domain_id: string,
// Normalised hostname of the custom domain.
hostname: string,
// ID of the page the route points at.
page_id: string,
// Normalised path on the domain ("/" for the domain root).
path: string,
// Unique route identifier.
route_id: string,
// True when the page has a published default revision and is actively serving content. False when the page has no published revision, so the route exists but visitors see nothing.
serves_content: boolean,
// Kind of resource the route points at.
target_type: "page",
// When the route was last updated.
updated_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// Full public URL of the route (https://{hostname}{path}).
url: string,
},
}>;
```

Use this tool to disconnect a custom-domain route from its Typeform Page, so that https://{domain}{path} stops serving the page.

## What this tool does
- Removes the route identified by route_id. The page itself and the custom domain are not affected.
- After disconnecting, the domain + path is free to be routed to another page with create_page_domain_route.

## Inputs
- route_id: ID of the route to disconnect (from create_page_domain_route or list_page_domain_routes).

## Output
- route_id: ID of the route that was disconnected.

## Notes
- Destructive: always confirm with the user before calling this tool. The public URL stops resolving immediately.
- There is no tool to restore a disconnected route; recreate it with create_page_domain_route.
- Returns ROUTE_NOT_FOUND when the route does not exist or was already disconnected.


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_disconnect_page_domain_route(args: {
// ID of the route to disconnect.
route_id: string,
}): Promise<{
// ID of the route that was disconnected.
route_id: string,
}>;
```

Use this tool to retrieve metadata and public URLs for a Typeform Page by ID. This returns page-level information only — not draft content or block structure.

## What this tool does
- Returns the page's id, title, workspace, timestamps, and resolved public URLs.
- Does not return block content, draft state, or variant data.

## Inputs
- page_id: the ID of the page to fetch.

## Output
- page: the page record with its public URLs.
  - links.display: the canonical URL shown to visitors.
  - links.default: the platform-assigned default URL.
  - links.custom_domain: custom domain URL, or null if none is configured.
  - links.builder: the Typeform admin URL where the user can edit this page in the builder (for example, to upload images). Give it to the user exactly as returned.
  - links.display is null until the page has been published.
- publication: whether the page is live, for its default variant.
  - default_variant_id: the variant this state describes.
  - status: empty_draft (nothing to publish yet), draft (never published), published (live, no newer edits) or changed (live, with unpublished edits).
  - is_live: true when status is published or changed.
  - has_unpublished_changes: true when status is changed.
  - live_revision_number: the revision visitors see, or null while not live.

## Notes
- Never construct builder or public URLs yourself from IDs. Page IDs and variant IDs look almost identical, and a builder URL built with a variant ID opens a broken builder. If links.builder is null, tell the user to open the page from the Pages dashboard.
- To read or edit a page's draft content, use the Typeform Pages draft editing tools.
- To list pages and obtain IDs, use list_pages.


```ts
