Use this tool to list Typeform Pages in an account, optionally scoped to a workspace and filtered by title. This is the recommended starting point — it returns the default_variant_id needed by all variant-scoped tools.

## What this tool does
- Returns one page of results (default 10, max 50 per page) ordered by most-recently-updated first, each with its public URLs.
- Returns default_variant_id for each page: the variantId expected by the Typeform Pages draft editing tools.
- Returns total_count so you know how many pages match across all result pages.

## Recommended workflow
1. Call list_pages (or create_page) to obtain a variantId (default_variant_id).
2. Use the Typeform Pages draft editing tools to read the page structure, discover block types, and edit the draft.
3. Call publish_variant to make the draft live.

## Inputs
- account_id: The Typeform account id of the caller making this request. Must be an account the caller has workspace membership in. Used for access checks and caller-specific entitlements (feature gating and usage attribution).

- workspace_id: optional. ID of the workspace to scope results. Pass null to list pages across the whole account.
- page_title: optional (null to skip). Case-insensitive substring match on the page title. Several pages can match, so check total_count and the returned titles.
- page: optional (null for 1). 1-based page number.
- page_size: optional (null for 10). Pages per result page, max 50.

## Output
- pages: the requested page of results, each with:
  - id, title, workspace_id, created_at, updated_at, links (public URLs, plus links.builder).
  - links.builder: the admin URL to edit the page in the builder; give it to the user exactly as returned.
  - default_variant_id: ID of the page's default variant. null when the page has no active default variant. It is NOT a page ID: never use it in builder or public URLs.
- total_count: total number of pages matching the filters, across all result pages.
- page, page_size: the page and page size applied.
- has_more: true when more results exist beyond this page.

## Notes
- To find a specific page, pass page_title. If has_more is true, call again with page + 1 or narrow page_title / workspace_id.


