Use this tool to publish a page variant, making the current draft live. This is the only tool that takes draft edits live — the Typeform Pages draft editing tools (add_block, update_block, set_theme, etc.) write to the draft only; the published page is unchanged until this tool is called.

## What this tool does
- Publishes the current draft of a variant as an immutable revision.
- The draft remains intact after publish — editing can continue immediately.

## Inputs
- page_id: the ID of the page that owns the variant.
- variant_id: the ID of the variant to publish.

## Output
- revision: the latest published revision, including:
  - the immutable content snapshot (json_snapshot). Its theme is { id }: the id of the applied page theme.
  - schema.org JSON-LD metadata generated from the snapshot.
  - the revision number and published timestamp.
- links: the page's public links (display, default, custom_domain). Any of them can be null.
- url: the public URL of the page now that it is live: links.display, or links.default when there is no display link. Null only when links could not be resolved.

## Behaviour
- If the variant has no unpublished changes, the existing latest revision is returned unchanged.
- If there are unpublished changes, a new immutable revision is created and returned.
- Repeating this request without further draft changes returns the same latest published revision.

## Response Guidelines
- Confirm that the publish request succeeded and the variant is up to date.
- Do not imply a new revision was created — it may have already been published with no changes.

## Notes
- Obtain variantId from list_pages (default_variant_id) or create_page (variant.id).


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_publish_variant(args: {
// ID of the page that owns the variant.
page_id: string,
// ID of the variant to publish.
variant_id: string,
}): Promise<{
links: {
// Region-aware admin URL where the page is edited in the builder (e.g. https://admin.typeform.com/accounts/{accountId}/pages/{id}/create). Present whether or not the page is live. Null when link resolution fails. Use verbatim; do not construct this URL from page or variant IDs.
builder: string | null,
// Active custom-domain URL. Null when the page is not live, when no active custom-domain route exists, or when link resolution fails.
custom_domain: string | null,
// Default subdomain URL (e.g. https://page.typeform.com/p/{id}). Null only when link resolution fails entirely.
