Use this tool to update the SEO or social metadata of a page variant draft.

## What this tool does
- Applies a batch of set/remove operations to the variant's metadata atomically.
- All operations are validated and dry-run before being written.
- Changes are to the draft only — not published.

## Inputs
- accountId: The Typeform account id of the caller making this request. Recorded as the author of the change. It is not used for access checks or feature gating. This may differ from the account that owns the Page when the caller is a collaborator on that page.
- variantId: The id of the variant whose metadata to update.
- ops: Array of operations. All are applied atomically — if any fails, none are written.

### Operations

**set** — Write or replace a metadata field.
- { op: "set", field: "title", value: "My Page | Typeform" }
- { op: "set", field: "show_in_search_results", value: false }

**remove** — Remove a metadata field.
- { op: "remove", field: "description" }

## Output
- metadata: The resulting metadata after all ops have been applied. All six fields are always present; null means the field is not set.

## Notes
- Call get_metadata_catalog first to discover the authoritative list of allowed fields and their constraints (maxLength, URL allowlist patterns).
- The field list is: title, description, site_name, favicon_url, social_image_url, show_in_search_results.
- favicon_url and social_image_url accept any public https URL that points directly to image bytes. Non-Typeform URLs are uploaded to the Typeform CDN and assigned to this variant; Typeform image URLs are assigned to this variant as they are. The output returns the resulting Typeform URL, not the one you sent.
- Local or pasted images (files on the user's device, or images pasted into the chat) cannot be sent through this tool: only public https URLs that point directly to image bytes work. Do not base64-encode them or invent a URL. When you do not have a real public image URL for a slot, keep using media-rich blocks and variants and set the image src to the placeholder https://public-assets.typeform.com/public/pages/pages-mcp-placeholder-image-v1.png instead of a stock image or leaving the slot out. Then tell the user that you added placeholder media because you cannot upload images yet, and that they can either swap it in the Typeform Pages builder or share a public image URL for you to use. If you have the page's links.builder URL (from the pages get_page, list_pages or create_page tools) or the user shared a builder link, give it to them proactively.
- Operations are applied in order; two ops on the same field are allowed (last one wins).

## Errors
- IMAGE_RESOLUTION_FAILED: an image URL is not https, cannot be fetched, or is not an image. The message names each failing field. No ops are written.
- METADATA_VIOLATION: a value breaks the field constraints (e.g. maxLength). No ops are written.


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_set_metadata(args: {
// The Typeform account id of the caller making this request. Recorded as the author of the change. It is not used for access checks or feature gating. This may differ from the account that owns the Page when the caller is a collaborator on that page.
accountId: string,
// Ordered list of set/remove operations to apply. Applied atomically after a dry-run validation pass.
ops: Array<

 | {
// A metadata field name. Consult get_metadata_catalog for the authoritative list of allowed fields and their constraints.
field: string,
op: "set",
// The value to set. Use a boolean for show_in_search_results; use a string for every other field.
// For favicon_url and social_image_url, any public https image URL is accepted. It is resolved to a Typeform CDN URL before it is written.
value: string | boolean,
}
 | {
// The metadata field to remove.
field: string,
op: "remove",
}

>,
// The variant whose live draft to update.
variantId: string,
}): Promise<{
// SEO and social metadata. All six fields are always present. String fields use null to mean "the field has not been explicitly set on the variant." show_in_search_results is always a concrete boolean.
metadata: {
// Used for <meta description> and og:description. Max 160 characters.
description: string | null,
// Favicon image URL. A Typeform CDN URL.
favicon_url: string | null,
// Drives the robots index/noindex directive. Always a concrete boolean.
show_in_search_results: boolean, // default: true
// Used for og:site_name.
site_name: string | null,
// Open Graph social image URL, typically 1200×630. A Typeform CDN URL.
social_image_url: string | null,
// Used for the <title> tag and og:title. Max 60 characters.
title: string | null,
},
}>;
```

Use this tool to update the page-level settings of a page variant draft.

## What this tool does
- Updates the provided settings fields on the variant's draft; fields you omit are left unchanged.
- Input is validated and dry-run before anything is written.
- Changes are to the draft only — not published.

## Inputs
- accountId: The Typeform account id of the caller making this request. Recorded as the author of the change. It is not used for access checks or feature gating. This may differ from the account that owns the Page when the caller is a collaborator on that page.
- variantId: The id of the variant whose settings to update.
- settings: Object of fields to change, e.g. { "hide_typeform_branding": true }.

## Output
- settings: The resulting settings after the update, with defaults resolved.

## Notes
- Call get_settings_catalog first to discover the authoritative list of settings and their types.
- Enabling hide_typeform_branding requires the page owner's account to have the pages-branding-removal entitlement (the calling account is irrelevant). If the owner's account lacks it, the call fails with FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE and nothing is written. If the entitlement cannot be verified (e.g. a transient outage), the call fails with FEATURE_CHECK_UNAVAILABLE, nothing is written, and it is safe to retry later.
- Setting hide_typeform_branding to false never requires the entitlement.


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_set_settings(args: {
// The Typeform account id of the caller making this request. Recorded as the author of the change. It is not used for access checks or feature gating. This may differ from the account that owns the Page when the caller is a collaborator on that page.
accountId: string,
// Settings to change. Only the provided fields are updated. Enabling hide_typeform_branding requires the page owner's account to have the pages-branding-removal entitlement.
settings: {
// Whether to hide the Typeform branding.
hide_typeform_branding: boolean,
},
// The variant whose live draft to update.
variantId: string,
}): Promise<{
// Page-level settings. Every field is always present; schema defaults are applied at read time.
settings: {
// Whether to hide the Typeform branding.
hide_typeform_branding: boolean, // default: false
},
}>;
```

