Use this tool to change the path of an existing custom-domain route, e.g. move a page from https://{domain}/ to https://{domain}/spring-sale.

## What this tool does
- Updates the path of the route identified by route_id. The domain and the target page stay the same.
- Idempotent: updating a route to its current path returns it unchanged.

## Inputs
- route_id: ID of the route to update (from create_page_domain_route or list_page_domain_routes).
- path: the new path. Either "/" for the domain root, or a single-segment alias of 5-15 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens (e.g. "/spring-sale"). Normalised to lowercase with a leading slash. Invalid paths return VALIDATION_ERROR.

## Output
- route: the updated route record:
  - route_id, domain_id, hostname, path, url (the full public URL), target_type ("page"), page_id.
  - serves_content: true when the routed page has a published revision and is serving content.
  - created_at, updated_at.
  - already_existed: present, and true, only when the requested domain and path were already routed to this page and no new route was created; omitted otherwise.

## Notes
- Destructive: always confirm with the user before calling this tool. The old URL stops resolving immediately after the update.
- Returns ROUTE_ALREADY_EXISTS when the new path is already used by another route on the same domain.
- Returns ROUTE_NOT_FOUND when the route does not exist or was disconnected.


```ts
mcp__Typeform__pages_public_update_page_domain_route(args: {
// New path for the route: "/" for the domain root, or a single-segment alias of 5-15 lowercase letters, digits or hyphens (e.g. "/spring-sale").
path: string,
// ID of the route to update.
route_id: string,
}): Promise<{
route: {
// Present, and true, only when the requested domain and path were already routed to this page and no new route was created. Omitted otherwise.
already_existed?: boolean,
// When the route was created.
created_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// ID of the custom domain (account-service page domain) this route is on.
domain_id: string,
// Normalised hostname of the custom domain.
hostname: string,
// ID of the page the route points at.
page_id: string,
// Normalised path on the domain ("/" for the domain root).
path: string,
// Unique route identifier.
route_id: string,
// True when the page has a published default revision and is actively serving content. False when the page has no published revision, so the route exists but visitors see nothing.
serves_content: boolean,
// Kind of resource the route points at.
target_type: "page",
// When the route was last updated.
updated_at: string, // format: "date-time"
// Full public URL of the route (https://{hostname}{path}).
url: string,
},
}>;
```

