Update an existing page theme owned by the authenticated user.

## What this tool does
Replaces the page theme identified by page_theme_id with the provided literal
values and returns the updated theme. This is a full replacement: every property
is overwritten, so omitted optional fields fall back to their defaults.

**Destructive: this is a full replacement. Omitted optional fields (e.g. logo,
background) are reset or cleared and the previous values cannot be recovered.**

## Inputs
- page_theme_id: the ID of the page theme to update (required).
- name: the page theme name (required).
- display_font: the font applied to display (heading) text (required).
- display_font_weight: the weight of the display font — "400", "500", "600", "700", or "900". Default "500".
- body_font: the font applied to body text (required).
- colors: text, button, button_content and background hex colors, e.g. "#1a2b3c" (required).
- background: an optional background image (href and brightness).
- logo: an optional logo (href required, optional alt_text, size "small"/"medium"/"large", placement "left"/"center"/"right").
- intro_text_alignment, main_text_alignment: "left" or "center". Default "left".
- rounded_corners: the Button corner radius — how rounded button corners are — "none", "small" or "large". Default "small".
- image_radius: the Media corner radius — how rounded image/media corners are — "none", "small" or "large". Default "none".

## Output
- page_theme: the updated page theme, with its id, name, display_font,
  display_font_weight, body_font, colors (text, button, button_content, background),
  optional background image (href, brightness), optional logo (href, alt_text, size,
  placement), intro_text_alignment, main_text_alignment, rounded_corners (Button corner
  radius), image_radius (Media corner radius), and visibility ("public" for Typeform
  system themes, "private" for user themes).


